1.01.099.940 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"src/addressable_information_layer/reopen.py\",\"start_line\":1}","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the task. I need to repair two regressions:\n\n1. `ArtifactUnit.start_line` and `end_line` are inclusive, so exact materialization must include every declared source line.\n2. `ReopenReceipt.truncated` is true only when the exact text is strictly longer than `max_chars`; equality is complete.\n\nI've already read `artifact_units.py`. Now I need to read `reopen.py`, `records.py`, and `hashing.py` before making mutations.\n\nLet me look at the code in `artifact_units.py` for the first issue:\n\nIn `exact_text_for_unit`:\n```python\ndef exact_text_for_unit(artifact: Artifact, unit: ArtifactUnit) -> str:\n    if unit.inline_text is not None:\n        return unit.inline_text\n    lines = artifact.text.splitlines()\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])\n```\n\nThe slice `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)]` — if start_line=1 and end_line=5, this gives `lines[0:4]` which is indices 0,1,2,3 — that's only 4 lines (lines 1-4), missing line 5. It should be `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : unit.end_line]` to include line `end_line`.\n\nAlso in `_make_unit`:\n```python\ntext = inline_text if inline_text is not None else (\"\\n\".join(lines[start_line - 1 : end_line]) if lines else artifact.text)\n```\nThis one correctly uses `lines[start_line - 1 : end_line]` which includes the end_line. So `_make_unit` is correct but `exact_text_for_unit` has the bug.\n\nThe fix for `exact_text_for_unit` should be:\n```python\nreturn \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : unit.end_line])\n```\n\nNow I need to read `reopen.py` to find the second issue with `ReopenReceipt.truncated`.\n\nLet me read the other files.\n"}
