1.47.523.078 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"src/addressable_information_layer/records.py\",\"start_line\":1}","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the task. I need to repair two regressions:\n\n1. `ArtifactUnit.start_line` and `end_line` are inclusive, so exact materialization must include every declared source line. Looking at `exact_text_for_unit`:\n```python\ndef exact_text_for_unit(artifact: Artifact, unit: ArtifactUnit) -> str:\n    if unit.inline_text is not None:\n        return unit.inline_text\n    lines = artifact.text.splitlines()\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])\n```\n\nThe issue here is the slice. `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)]` — this uses `end_line - 1` as the stop index, but Python slicing is exclusive at the end. So if `start_line=1` and `end_line=5`, it would slice `lines[0:4]` which gives lines 1-4, missing line 5. The correct slice should be `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : unit.end_line]` to include all lines from start_line to end_line inclusive.\n\n2. `ReopenReceipt.truncated` is true only when the exact text is strictly longer than `max_chars`; equality is complete. Looking at:\n```python\ntruncated = len(exact_text) >= max_chars\n```\n\nThis should be `len(exact_text) > max_chars` (strictly greater than). Equality means complete, not truncated.\n\nLet me also check the other files to make sure I have the full picture before patching. I need to read `records.py` and `hashing.py` as instructed. But actually, I already have the exact source of `artifact_units.py` and `reopen.py`. Let me read the other two files to be thorough as instructed.\n\nActually, let me just proceed with the patches since I can clearly see the two bugs:\n\n1. In `artifact_units.py`, line with `exact_text_for_unit`:\n   - Current: `return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])`\n   - Should be: `return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : unit.end_line])`\n\n2. In `reopen.py`:\n   - Current:"}
