2.43.587.699 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"src/addressable_information_layer/hashing.py\",\"start_line\":1}","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the task. I need to repair two regressions in the exact-reopen pipeline:\n\n1. `ArtifactUnit.start_line` and `end_line` are inclusive, so exact materialization must include every declared source line.\n2. `ReopenReceipt.truncated` is true only when the exact text is strictly longer than `max_chars`; equality is complete.\n\nLet me look at the current code:\n\n**In `artifact_units.py`, the `exact_text_for_unit` function:**\n```python\ndef exact_text_for_unit(artifact: Artifact, unit: ArtifactUnit) -> str:\n    if unit.inline_text is not None:\n        return unit.inline_text\n    lines = artifact.text.splitlines()\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])\n```\n\nThe issue here: `end_line` is inclusive, so to get line `end_line`, we need the slice to go up to index `end_line - 1` (0-based), which means the slice should be `[start_line - 1 : end_line]` (since Python slices are exclusive at the end). The current code uses `max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)` as the upper bound, which would exclude the last line when `end_line > start_line`. For example, if `start_line=1, end_line=5`, the correct slice is `[0:5]` giving lines 1-5. But the current code gives `[0:4]` giving only lines 1-4.\n\nThe fix: change `max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)` to `unit.end_line`.\n\n**In `reopen.py`, the truncation logic:**\n```python\ntruncated = len(exact_text) >= max_chars\nmaterialized = exact_text[:max_chars] if truncated else exact_text\n```\n\nThe issue: `truncated` should be true only when the text is *strictly longer* than `max_chars`. The current code uses `>=` which means equality (text length == max_chars) would incorrectly mark it as truncated. The fix is to change `>=` to `>`.\n\nLet me also check `hashing.py` - I haven't read it yet. Let me read it first before making changes. Actually, let me re-read the task: \"Inspect exact"}
