e first fix I already made was correct. The original code was:\n```python\nreturn \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])\n```\n\nThe issue: `end_line` is inclusive, so to get lines from `start_line` to `end_line` (inclusive), we need indices `start_line - 1` to `end_line` (exclusive end in Python slice). The original used `max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)` which would be off-by-one (excluding the last line). My fix changed it to `unit.end_line` which is correct for an inclusive end.\n\nNow I need to patch `reopen.py`. The current candidate is `f1cb476bed"}
