8.44.861.571 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"src/addressable_information_layer/reopen.py\",\"start_line\":1}","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the task. I need to repair two regressions:\n\n1. `ArtifactUnit.start_line` and `end_line` are inclusive, so exact materialization must include every declared source line.\n2. `ReopenReceipt.truncated` is true only when the exact text is strictly longer than `max_chars`; equality is complete.\n\nI've already read `artifact_units.py`. Now I need to read `reopen.py`, `records.py`, and `hashing.py` before making mutations.\n\nLet me look at what I've already seen in `artifact_units.py`:\n\nIn `exact_text_for_unit`:\n```python\ndef exact_text_for_unit(artifact: Artifact, unit: ArtifactUnit) -> str:\n    if unit.inline_text is not None:\n        return unit.inline_text\n    lines = artifact.text.splitlines()\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])\n```\n\nThe issue here: `end_line` is inclusive, so to include line `end_line`, we need `lines[start-1:end]` (since Python slicing is exclusive at the end). But the current code uses `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)]`. \n\nIf start_line=5 and end_line=10, then:\n- We want lines 5 through 10 (inclusive), which is indices 4 through 9.\n- Python slice for that would be `lines[4:10]` or equivalently `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : unit.end_line]`.\n- But the current code does `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)]` which gives `lines[4:9]`, missing line 10.\n\nSo the fix for `exact_text_for_unit` is to change `unit.end_line - 1` to `unit.end_line`.\n\nNow I need to read `reopen.py` to find the second regression about `ReopenReceipt.truncated`. Let me read that file.\n"}
