9.29.613.698 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"{\"action\":\"read\",\"path\":\"src/addressable_information_layer/records.py\",\"start_line\":1}","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the task. I need to repair two regressions:\n\n1. `ArtifactUnit.start_line` and `end_line` are inclusive, so exact materialization must include every declared source line.\n2. `ReopenReceipt.truncated` is true only when the exact text is strictly longer than `max_chars`; equality is complete.\n\nLet me look at the current code:\n\nIn `artifact_units.py`, the `exact_text_for_unit` function:\n```python\ndef exact_text_for_unit(artifact: Artifact, unit: ArtifactUnit) -> str:\n    if unit.inline_text is not None:\n        return unit.inline_text\n    lines = artifact.text.splitlines()\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)])\n```\n\nThe issue here: `unit.end_line` is inclusive, so to include line `end_line`, we need the slice to go up to `end_line` (exclusive in Python slicing). The correct slice should be `lines[start_line - 1 : end_line]`. \n\nCurrent code: `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : max(unit.start_line - 1, unit.end_line - 1)]`\n\nThis is wrong because:\n- `unit.end_line - 1` would exclude the last line (since Python slices are exclusive at the end)\n- The correct slice for inclusive start/end is `lines[start_line - 1 : end_line]`\n\nSo the fix is: `lines[unit.start_line - 1 : unit.end_line]`\n\nIn `reopen.py`, the truncation logic:\n```python\ntruncated = len(exact_text) >= max_chars\n```\n\nThis should be:\n```python\ntruncated = len(exact_text) > max_chars\n```\n\nBecause \"truncated is true only when the exact text is strictly longer than max_chars; equality is complete.\"\n\nLet me also check `records.py` and `hashing.py` before making changes. Let me read those files first.\n\nActually, I already have the source for `artifact_units.py` and `reopen.py`. Let me read `records.py` and `hashing.py` to be thorough, then make the patches.\n"}
